# Default-deny context keeps local experiments, worktrees, caches and raw
# results out even when they use a name that has not appeared in this
# repository before. Containerfile.cuda installs this repo's two
# distributions from source -- core (pyproject.toml at the root, whose
# package-dir maps jittor.src -> src/ and jittor.backends.* -> backends/*/)
# and compat (compat/pyproject.toml) -- plus runs its pytest suite, so both
# distributions' full source and the test tree need to reach the build
# context, not just the plain `python/` package the old single-distribution
# image needed.
**
!setup.py
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!MANIFEST.in
!LICENSE.txt
!AGENTS.md
!python/
!python/**
!src/
!src/**
!backends/
!backends/**
!compat/
!compat/**
!tests/
!tests/**
!tools/
!tools/**
!agent/
!agent/**
!requirements/
!requirements/**
!examples/
!examples/**
examples/**/__pycache__/
examples/**/.pytest_cache/
examples/**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
examples/**/*.ipynb
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.pyc
